        "description": "<div id=\"remove_no_follow\">\n\t\t<div class=\"grid grid--cols-10@md grid--cols-8@lg article-column \">\n\t\t\t\t\t  <div class=\"col-12 col-10@md col-6@lg col-start-3@lg\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"article-column__content\">\n<section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This series lays out a practical framework for taking generative AI (GenAI) from pilots to dependable production systems in the enterprise. It focuses on four disciplines that determine long-term success: engineering for scale and reliability, designing agentic systems with clear constraints, embedding governance directly into build and runtime controls, and measuring ROI at the workflow level with full cost and outcome visibility. The throughline is operational discipline\u2014treating GenAI as a service with contracts, evaluation, ownership, and measurable business impact.</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"extendedBlock-wrapper block-coreImage undefined\"><figure data-wp-context='{\"image",
